1. Convert homepage to Next.js/React with mock data
2. Set up basic database + backend routes
3. Connect one workflow end-to-end
4. Then continue building more pages


The first end-to-end workflow should be very small:

Add Term button
↓
Submit term form
↓
POST /api/terms
↓
Save to SQLite
↓
GET /api/terms
↓
Show term card on Dashboard

***
Phase 1: Next.js setup
- Create Next.js project
- Move homepage into app/page.tsx
- Reuse your existing CSS
- Use fake term data first

Phase 2: Backend/database foundation
- Add Prisma
- Use SQLite locally
- Create Term, Course, GradeComponent models
- Add API route for terms

Phase 3: First real workflow
- Dashboard loads terms from database
- Add Term modal saves to database
- Delete Term removes from database

Phase 4: Continue pages
- Term page
- Course page
- Grade components
- GPA calculations



